"""Private build audit; BIND-MOUNT it, never add it to the agent image: it carries what it looks for.

Asserts that no withheld implementation is recoverable from the image: neither the withheld
upstream implementation nor its later fixes, and not the FlashAttention fork's per-sequence
phases at or after its first such change, in source, installed code, bytecode, archives or caches.

* Markers: the withheld identifiers, generated by rule (prepare_fa_vendor.py --identifiers: every
  def/class name and string constant of 12 or more characters on a line those changes add, kept iff
  absent from every pristine root, plus the named identifiers) and frozen here. Scanned in the
  working tree, all installed packages, /public, /opt, /root, /tmp, /usr/local/lib, /var/cache and
  the checkpoint's text files; tensor payloads are excluded.
* Blobs: every file content those changes produce that neither the base's history nor the vendored
  fork also contains, by git blob id -- absent from /app's object store.
* The object store: every object is reachable from HEAD (no unreachable object, no ref outside
  HEAD's history, no alternates). Objects reachable from the base commit are upstream's history at
  the base, fixed by its SHA and older than that implementation; the objects the two preparation
  commits add are scanned for the markers like any file.

--filesystem-only scans individual image layers before their whiteouts are applied.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import bz2
